  "_comment": "Fixture identical in shape to bindinginfo_cdict.json (including the `owned::Int32` ownership field), but instantiated at V=Int32 instead of V=Float64 — proves cdict_struct_info's value-type parameterization (and the helper codegen that substitutes the matching ctypes name) varies correctly beyond a single value type. Field offsets (0, 8, 16, 24, size 32) are IDENTICAL to the Float64 case: `values` is a pointer field (8 bytes) regardless of what it points at, so the pointee's own size never affects CDict's own layout. `keys`/`jlw_free_strings` are unaffected by the value type (always Ptr{CString}); only `values`'s pointee type and the Float64->Int32 substitution in from_dict/as_dict's value ctype differ from bindinginfo_cdict.json.",
